From: klee <71413974+kleeedolinux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:50:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] render: covered windows get frame callbacks at most every 33
 ms or 2 updates when more than 10 windows are open

New misc keys: throttle_occluded, throttle_window_count, throttle_occlusion_cutoff, throttle_freeze_ms,
throttle_freeze_updates, reconfigure_ack_timeout_ms, frame_deadline.

A window above counts as an occluder with its whole box when its surface is
opaque, else with the extents of its opaque region (rounded corners and CSD
shadows make the surface non-opaque but leave the region over the content);
faded or translucent windows cover nothing. Under a fullscreen window only the
windows Hyprland hides there are covered: dialogs, popups and pinned windows
allowed over it keep their frames. WolosPerf::occluderRect and
coveredByFullscreen, gtest in tests/helpers/WolosPerf.cpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
